# Build context hygiene. Anything not needed to RUN the API is excluded, both to
# shrink the image and to keep the context upload fast.
.venv*/
venv/
.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
notebooks/
tests/
docs/
outputs/
*.md
!README.md
.env

# NOT excluded, deliberately: app/ and report/.
# Hugging Face builds EVERY Space as a Docker image and honours this file, and
# the Streamlit Space is built from this same repo. Excluding app/ here took the
# live app down with "File does not exist: app/streamlit_app.py"; excluding
# report/ would strip the figures the app renders (app/_shared.py resolves
# FIG_DIR to report/figures). The API's Dockerfile simply does not COPY them, so
# they cost build-context transfer (~3 MB) and nothing in the image.

# Data: exclude everything EXCEPT the three small committed 360K artifacts
# (~7.7 MB) that the service reads at startup. Crucially this keeps the 514 MiB
# ease_B.npy out of the image -- it is fetched at boot instead (see
# scripts/fetch_ease_b.py), which is the whole point of the deployment design.
data/*
!data/processed
data/processed/*
!data/processed/lastfm360k
data/processed/lastfm360k/*
!data/processed/lastfm360k/matrix.npz
!data/processed/lastfm360k/item_ids.parquet
!data/processed/lastfm360k/user_ids.parquet
